            "question": "How do I attach glass railing to a wood deck over a canyon?",
            "answer": "<p>Two ways. The 6-inch top-mount spigot fixes to the deck surface over solid blocking. The side-mount spigot fixes to the rim joist or fascia, which keeps the deck surface clear on a narrow canyon deck. Our <a href=\"/pages/glass-railing-engineering-testing\">engineering documents</a> show the testing and the blocking details for both spigots on wood and on concrete. Screws and bolts are sold separately.</p>",
