            "question": "Can I put a glass railing on my Coronado or downtown condo balcony?",
            "answer": "<p>Usually, with two approvals: the building department and your HOA or condo board. The California code sets 42 inches as the minimum guard height; the 39.6-inch panel gives that and the 46-inch panel gives 48 inches. The 6-inch top-mount spigot fits a concrete balcony, and wall connectors finish at the stucco. Freight delivery is to the curb with a liftgate, so plan how to bring the panels up.</p>",
